Match the real "Noto Sans Symbols 2" family name in the unix fallback list.

The family name of Noto Sans Symbols 2 contains a space, but cosmic-text's unix
fallback list only carries the unspaced "Noto Sans Symbols2" spelling. fontdb
matches family names exactly, so that entry never resolves to the installed font.

U+23FA (BLACK CIRCLE FOR RECORD, Claude Code's message/tool bullet) is a
text-presentation symbol that lives in that family and is missing from the
Noto/DejaVu families listed ahead of it, so without this it falls through to Noto
Color Emoji and renders as a filled color block.

The symbol fonts this reaches cover technical/text symbols but not pictographic
emoji, so real emoji (e.g. U+1F534) still resolve to the color emoji font.

--- a/src/font/fallback/unix.rs
+++ b/src/font/fallback/unix.rs
@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@
         /* Symbols fallbacks */
         "Noto Sans Symbols",
         "Noto Sans Symbols2",
+        // The Noto Sans Symbols 2 family name actually contains a space; the
+        // unspaced spelling above doesn't match it in fontdb. U+23FA (Claude
+        // Code's bullet) lives here, so without this it falls through to the
+        // color emoji font and renders as a filled block.
+        "Noto Sans Symbols 2",
         /* Emoji fallbacks*/
         "Noto Color Emoji",
         //TODO: Add CJK script here for doublewides?
